    "id": "cs-big-o-growth-curves",
    "title": "Big-O Complexity Growth Curves",
    "field": "Computer Science / Algorithms",
    "plotType": "Multi-line plot of operation count vs. input size, one line per complexity class",
    "description": "Overlaid curves show how the number of basic operations grows with input size n for each Big-O complexity class: O(1), O(log n), O(n), O(n log n), and O(n^2). Plotting them together makes the divergence obvious — the flat and logarithmic curves stay near the bottom while quadratic growth shoots up steeply. It is a reference chart for reasoning about how an algorithm will scale before you ever run it.",
